From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rmtfs.service: store the EFS images in /var/lib/rmtfs

The packaged unit starts rmtfs with "-r -P -s", i.e. it goes looking for raw EFS
partitions on the device.  On the Xiaomi Book S 12.4 those are not usable (the
modem runs the no-modem firmware), so the images have to live in a directory
instead - which is what "-o <dir>" is for, and what this board has been running
with as a hand-written /etc/systemd/system/rmtfs.service override:

    ExecStart=/usr/bin/rmtfs -r -s -o /var/lib/rmtfs

Fold that into the unit so the override is not needed.  -r (read-only) stays: the
modem never writes back, and read-only keeps a stale EFS from turning into a
corrupt one.  -P goes away with the partition lookup.  RMTFS_EFS_PATH is
substituted by the Makefile and defaults to /var/lib/rmtfs, which the package
also creates through tmpfiles.d.

Upstream ships a second unit (rmtfs-dir.service) that already passes -o, but it
does not pass -r and is not what the main unit should be here.
---
diff --git a/rmtfs.service.in b/rmtfs.service.in
index f7df549..4e42ed4 100644
--- a/rmtfs.service.in
+++ b/rmtfs.service.in
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ Before=NetworkManager.service
 ConditionPathExists=/dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1
 
 [Service]
-ExecStart=RMTFS_PATH/rmtfs -r -P -s
+ExecStart=RMTFS_PATH/rmtfs -r -s -o RMTFS_EFS_PATH
 Restart=always
 RestartSec=1
 
